  "worked_solution": "We know that the line passes through the point $(2,4),$ so we can use $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(2,4)$ in our point-slope formula. All that remains is to compute $m,$ and we can do this using the given points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}=\\frac{(-8)-4}{(-4)-2}=\\frac{-12}{-6}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $m=2$ and the point $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(2,4)$ into the point-slope formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-4 & =2(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
